From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 04d0: straight-line vertex fetch (Direct3D 12): the shared memory binding is chosen when the vertex shader is translated, and the endian swap has no branches (dxbc_vs_straight_fetch)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (O3; changes R8-A and R8-B of $WORK/scratch/R8/REPORT.md and patch_spec.md, whose
  variants/src is the working prototype; the result is byte-identical to it, see below). The DXBC translator it changes is
  Xenia's (Triang3l, BSD-3-Clause) in the ReXGlue SDK. Not run in the game: built (SDK build of the series with this
  patch, scratch tree $WORK/scratch/O3), run offline on the 1,061 translations of the E2 shader storage (the harness below),
  compiled by RGA for gfx1150, and the swap executed on random words, nothing more
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: R8 found that the cost of a vertex shader on the Radeon 880M is latency, not ALU: every vfetch sits in its own basic
  blocks (a uniform `if` on the system flag kSysFlag_SharedMemoryIsUAV to read the shared memory from the SRV or from the
  UAV, then two endian switches), so each vertex load is followed by a full wait before the next one is issued; a shadow
  vertex shader does about 7 dependent memory round trips, a colour one about 13. Cvar dxbc_vs_straight_fetch (bool, hot
  reload, default false until a run has validated it; the profile turns it on) makes the vertex fetch straight-line code:
  * R8-A, the binding: with the cvar on, a vertex shader that fetches vertices is translated for the binding the shared memory
    has in the draw that asks for it, the one the system flag says now: UAV in a draw that uses memexport (the draw's
    memexport_used: its vertex or its pixel shader exports), SRV otherwise. The ld_raw is emitted once, from that binding,
    with no flag test and no if / else. Both bindings are still declared and allocated (as the stock code does after its
    `if`), so the resources, the root signature and the descriptors are the same. The choice is a bit of the vertex shader
    modification (Modification::vertex.shared_memory_is_uav, set only with the cvar on and only for a shader with vertex
    fetches), made in D3D12CommandProcessor::IssueDraw from memexport_used and passed to
    PipelineCache::GetCurrentVertexShaderModification. Pixel shaders keep the run-time branch (they don't fetch vertices).
  * R8-B, the swap: the vertex fetch's endian swap (Endian128 from the fetch constant) and the vertex index's (Endian, from
    the system constant) are the new DxbcShaderTranslator::EmitStraightEndianSwap: the 8-in-16 byte swap
    ((x << 8) & 0xFF00FF00 | (x >> 8) & 0x00FF00FF) and the 16-in-32 rotation (bfi), always computed and selected with movc
    on ((e + 1) & 2) and (e & 2), which are uniform in the draw, instead of two switches on e (and the umad x * 256 + y that
    kept the compiler from forming a v_perm). Exactly the same value for e = 0 ... 3. The memexport's own 64/128-bit swaps are
    not touched.
  Each alone changes little (R8: the other leaves block boundaries around every fetch); together the shader is one basic block
  from the fetch to the first use and the compiler issues all the vertex loads and constant loads before the first wait.
  R8's numbers (RGA gfx1150, dynamic path): serial memory rounds 6.8 -> 4.2 (shadow VS, -38 %) and 12.8 -> 7.4 (colour VS,
  -42 %); SALU -19 / -23 %, v_mul_lo_u32 5.3 -> 1.0 (shadow), static branches 8.4 -> 4.0. Expected 0.1-0.3 ms in the
  shadow pass and 0.1-0.4 ms in the main view at 1080p [INFERENCE, R8], to be benched.
  What the cvar keys, and kVersion: the option is not read by the translation: it is two bits of the vertex shader
  modification (vs_straight_fetch and shared_memory_is_uav, in the free upper bits of the second dword, set by
  DxbcShaderTranslator::ApplyVertexShaderOptimizations from the cvar and the draw when the draw makes its modification). The
  modification is the key of the translation (Shader::translations_), of the pipeline (PipelineDescription.
  vertex_shader_modification, hashed) and of the stored pipeline description (.xpso), so a setting of the cvar (and a draw that
  uses memexport) never reuses the DXBC, the pipeline or the stored description of another one, however and whenever the cvar
  is changed (a change makes new translations and pipelines, compiled on first use: one stutter). All bits 0 is the stock
  modification, so Modification::kVersion and the storage versions are NOT bumped (R8's spec bumped kVersion, because it set
  the binding bit for every vertex shader; with the cvar as the first bit the old stored descriptions are the cvar-off ones and
  stay valid) and the shader storage (.xsh) is not affected. At the start-up preload, a stored vertex shader description whose
  vs_straight_fetch differs from the cvar's is not translated and so its pipeline is not made (the stored shared_memory_is_uav
  is kept: only a draw knows it): the .xpso keeps the entries of both settings and a run builds only its own. A vertex shader
  used with and without memexport has two translations with the cvar on (none seen in the E2 corpus).
  This is not the 04b0 pixel shader options (it needs nothing of them). Vertex shaders keep refactoring off (R8-C is not done:
  it breaks position invariance), the SM3 zero-multiply emulation stays, and the Vulkan translator is untouched.
Bucket: REDO

04d0-vs-straight-fetch.patch (mcla-x86 O3; R8 of $WORK/scratch/R8/REPORT.md)

Changed files: include/rex/graphics/pipeline/shader/dxbc_translator.h (Modification::vertex bits, ApplyVertexShaderOptimizations,
EmitStraightEndianSwap, the accessors), include/rex/graphics/d3d12/pipeline_cache.h, src/graphics/pipeline/shader/
{dxbc_translator.cpp (the cvar, the two functions, the vertex index swap), dxbc_translator_fetch.cpp (the vertex fetch)},
src/graphics/d3d12/{pipeline_cache.cpp (the modification, the preload skip), command_processor.cpp (memexport_used passed)}. No new
files; Vulkan untouched. The pixel shaders and everything the cvar leaves off are translated exactly as before.

Checks done (scratch tree $WORK/scratch/O3 = series 92 + this patch):
  * python tools/prepare_sdk.py --work $WORK/scratch/O3 build (Release): builds and installs.
  * Harness (scratch/O3/harness/harness_o3.cpp, linked with the objects of that build) over the 1,061 (shader, modification)
    pairs of the E2 storage, AMD, bindless, RTV: cvar off: 1,061 of 1,061 byte-identical to the stock translation (R1's out/).
    Cvar on: all 440 vertex shaders change, the 621 pixel shaders don't, and the 201 vertex + 112 pixel translations of R8's
    ss3 prototype set (R8's R8_VSRV=1 R8_VSWAP=3) are byte-identical to R8's out_ss3. With the draw using memexport (--uav) the same
    translations read U0 where the others read T0 (both declared in both).
  * scratch/O3/harness/swaptest.cpp executes the emitted DXBC (a small interpreter of the integer instructions, temporaries,
    immediates and switch / case that the sequences use) for the endianness 0, 1, 2, 3, for 20,000 random words (and 0, ~0,
    0x01020304, 0x80000001) per write mask for each of the 15 masks of the fetch (the endianness in the scratch register's unused
    component, or in another register for 0xF) and 200,000 for the vertex index (r0.x, scratch r0.y), against an independent C
    reference (8-in-16, 8-in-32 = bswap, 16-in-32 = swap of the halves), also for the stock switch sequence emitted by the same
    assembler, and checking that nothing else (the other components, the endianness) is touched:
    4,000,000 executions, 0 failures (12 instructions).
  * RGA 2.15, DX12 live driver, gfx1150, R8's job lists (81 depth-only vertex shaders with no pixel shader, 54 of them the shadow
    ones, and 120 colour vertex shaders with their pixel shaders), run under the heavy lock: every job compiled (0 failed of 81 + 120). Mean per shader against the stock translation (R8's rga_base: the same driver and job lists), shadow 54: serial memory rounds 6.8 -> 4.2, SALU 61.4 -> 49.6, VALU 231 -> 223, static branches 8.4 -> 4.0, v_mul_lo_u32 5.3 -> 1.0, VGPR 23.1 -> 22.1; the other 27 depth-only: rounds 6.2 -> 4.1, SALU 57.9 -> 47.7; colour 120: rounds 12.8 -> 7.4, vertex loads
    waited on in 2.7 -> 0.8 rounds, SALU 105 -> 81, VALU 410 -> 394, branches 15.9 -> 6.9, v_mul_lo_u32 8.2 -> 1.1, VGPR 39.6 -> 39.0 - R8's numbers, and the ISA statistics are identical to those of R8's ss3 (the same DXBC). Five of them translated for a memexport draw (--uav) compile too, with the same rounds.
  * Not run: the game, a picture, the stored-pipeline preload and the pipeline creation.

Checks to run (VER), in this order (profile cvar: dxbc_vs_straight_fetch=true):
  1. Cvar false: the pipeline storage and the picture as before.
  2. Cvar true: no shader or pipeline creation failure in the log; a frozen frame and a moving scene against the stock ones:
     identical (the same values), including the rain / vinyl / any draw that uses memexport (the UAV translation).
  3. GPU time of the shadow pass and of the whole frame (n1080 A/B pair, GT build for per-pass deltas; the gain is per draw
     segment, so larger with clear_memory_page_state=true).
  4. A toggle between runs on the same cache: "Created N graphics pipelines ... from the storage" counts only the pipelines of that
     run's setting (the other's entries stay in the .xpso unused); a setting not seen before compiles at first use, and a second
     run preloads it.

